; A map whose members all load and check, and whose ALIGNMENT NAMES A CLAIM NO
; MEMBER DECLARES. Resolution decides nothing about the members — it only asks
; whether the manifest's coordinates name anything at all — so this is an
; ill-formed map (exit 2), not a rejection.
;
; It is the second `pre-boundary` anchor for scripts/check-map-conformance.sh,
; and the one that pins the other exit code: reference resolution runs on both
; the `check` and the `map-input` door, before either produces anything, so the
; two must refuse identically and neither may emit an envelope. Were the two
; doors to disagree here, a manifest could be turned into bytes the Lean driver
; would then be asked to reproduce a verdict for.
(lara-map@1
  (policy empirical-v1 ../agreement/empirical-v1.policy.lara)
  (backends (backend nd 1))
  (members
    (member paper_pos ../agreement/pos.lara)
    (member paper_neg ../agreement/neg.lara))
  (alignments
    (alignment
      (ref paper_pos c_pos whole)
      (ref paper_neg c_missing whole)
      different
      (author reviewer_r)
      (audit-status unreviewed)
      (rationale "The right-hand coordinate names a claim paper_neg does not declare.")))
  (questions))
